# ECS Module

## Purpose

Provides the Entity-Component-System architecture for the game layer. `ECSRegistry` is the central store. Systems operate on components each frame. Resource-heavy objects (meshes, materials, physics bodies, sounds) are held in `ResourceStore` pools and referenced by opaque `ResourceId` values. Creator ownership for meshes/materials uses RAII `ResourceHandle`.

## Key Classes

| Class | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `ComponentPool<T>` | Sparse-set dense storage per component type; cache-friendly iteration over `mDense` |
| `ECSRegistry` | Type-erased component store; template API for compile-time safety; uses `std::type_index` -> `ComponentPool<T>` internally |
| `ResourceStore<PtrType>` | Id-keyed, ref-counted store for smart-pointer resources |
| `ResourceHandle` | RAII owner of one store ref (`Adopt` after `Store`; copy AddReferences; destroy/Reset RemoveReferences) |
| `TransformComponent` | Position / rotation / scale with dirty-flag caching; world matrix updated by `SceneGraphSystem` |
| `SceneGraphComponent` | Parent entity ID + children list; drives hierarchical transform propagation |
| `RenderComponent` | Holds non-owning `ResourceId`s for mesh, material, descriptor, uniform buffer; `texture_index` for bindless sampling; `uv_rect` for animation sub-regions; visibility flag |
| `PhysicsComponent` | Holds body `ResourceId`; event queue for forces/impulses/velocity/position/rotation/sleep |
| `BoxColliderComponent` / `CircleColliderComponent` | Collision shape + `CollisionFilter` (category/mask/group bits) |
| `AudioSourceComponent` | Named sound source map (`string` -> `ResourceId` for `SoundPool`) |
| `AudioEventComponent` | Queue of Play/Stop/Pause/Resume events keyed by source name |
| `AnimatedSpriteComponent` | Per-entity sprite animation state: `clip_id`, frame index, elapsed time, playing/loop/finished |
| `EffectInstanceComponent` | Marks a pooled FX entity; `effect_id` is an EffectSystem definition (not a clip), `active` for recycle |
| `HudTransformComponent` | Normalized screen position (0-1) + pixel offset + anchor enum |
| `HudTextComponent` | Text string + font size for ImGui HUD rendering |
| `HudBarComponent` | Progress bar value/max for HUD rendering |
| `RenderSystem` | Creates Vulkan mesh/material resources; uploads textures to bindless array; attaches `RenderComponent`; syncs camera state |
| `PhysicsSystem` | Wraps `PhysicsEngine`; creates Box2D bodies; processes physics event queue; dispatches collision events via `Observer` |
| `AudioSystem` | Loads sound pools; processes `AudioEventComponent` queue each frame |
| `AnimationSystem` | Loads/caches `AnimationClip` assets; drives `AnimatedSpriteComponent` playback each frame |
| `EffectSystem` | Pools fire-and-forget FX entities; `Create` returns effect `ResourceId` (clip list + pool); `Apply(id, pos)` plays primary clip |
| `SceneGraphSystem` | Traverses parent-child hierarchy; propagates world matrices top-down |
| `SceneResourceLoader` | (assets module) Preloads scene manifest; not an ECS tick system -- used at scene enter |

## ECSRegistry API

```cpp
Entity entity = registry.CreateEntity();
registry.AddComponent<TransformComponent>( entity, TransformComponent{ ... } );

if( registry.HasComponent<RenderComponent>( entity ) )
{
    auto& render = registry.GetComponent<RenderComponent>( entity );
}

// Iterate all entities with a given component type (dense array walk)
for( auto [entity, transform] : registry.GetComponentMap<TransformComponent>() )
{
    // ...
}

registry.RemoveComponent<TransformComponent>( entity );
```

## ResourceStore + ResourceHandle API

```cpp
ResourceId id = store.Store( std::make_unique<MyResource>( ... ) );
ResourceHandle handle = ResourceHandle::Adopt( store, id ); // owns the Store's initial ref

ResourceHandle copy = handle; // AddReference
handle.Reset();               // RemoveReference

MyResource* ptr = store.Get( handle.Get() ); // nullptr if invalid
bool live = store.Exists( id );
```

Ownership: handles (and attach/detach) own refs. `RenderComponent` stores non-owning `ResourceId`s. Physics bodies use the Store initial ref as the component-owned ref until `OnEntityDestroying`.

## RenderSystem API (sprites)

```cpp
uint32_t tex_index = render_system.CreateTexture( "./resources/textures/ship/Ship.png" );

MaterialHandle mat = render_system.CreateMaterial( MaterialBuilder()
    .SetShaders( "vert.spv", "frag.spv" )
    .SetAlphaBlending()
    .Build() );

MeshHandle mesh = render_system.CreateSpriteMesh( 32.f, 32.f );

render_system.AttachRenderable( entity, mesh.Get(), mat.Get(), tex_index );
// Keep mesh/mat handles alive while shared; Reset() when dropping creator ownership.

// AttachSprite creates a per-entity mesh and leaves the entity as sole mesh owner
render_system.AttachSprite( entity, mat.Get(), 32.f, 32.f, tex_index );
```

## Physics Event Queue Pattern

Game logic queues physics commands on the component; `PhysicsSystem::Update()` drains the queue:

```cpp
auto& phys = registry.GetComponent<PhysicsComponent>( entity );
phys.QueueImpulse( { 0.f, 100.f, 0.f } );
phys.QueueSetVelocity( { 0.f, 0.f, 0.f } );
// Processed next PhysicsSystem::Update()
```

## Audio Event Queue Pattern

```cpp
auto& audio_event = registry.GetComponent<AudioEventComponent>( entity );
audio_event.events.push_back( { "thruster", AudioEvent::Type::Play } );
// Processed next AudioSystem::Update()
```

## Collision Callbacks (PhysicsSystem::Observer)

```cpp
class MyListener : public PhysicsSystem::Observer
{
    void OnCollideBegin( Entity a, Entity b ) override { /* hit logic */ }
    void OnSensorEnter( Entity sensor, Entity other ) override { /* trigger zone */ }
};

physics_system.RegisterObserver( &my_listener );
```

## Key Patterns

- **Event queueing:** Components accumulate commands during logic phase; systems drain them during `Update()`. Prevents mid-frame state corruption.
- **ResourceId indirection:** ECS never stores raw graphics/physics/audio pointers. Use `ResourceStore::Get()` to resolve, check for `nullptr`.
- **Handle ownership:** Systems hold `ResourceHandle` for shared meshes/materials; entities get refs via `AttachRenderable` / lose them via `DetachRenderable`.
- **PIMPL in RenderSystem:** Public header has no Vulkan includes. All Vulkan types live in the `.cpp` impl struct.
- **Dirty-flag transforms:** Only recompute local matrix when `TransformComponent` is modified. `SceneGraphSystem` propagates world matrices.
- **Unit conversion:** `PhysicsSystem` converts pixels <-> meters internally. Game code always works in pixel units.
- **Texture decoupling:** `CreateTexture()` returns a bindless index; materials define shader/pipeline state only. Multiple entities can share one material with different `texture_index` values.

## DOs

- Queue physics commands via `PhysicsComponent::Queue*()` -- never modify Box2D bodies directly
- Use `registry.GetComponentMap<T>()` to iterate all entities with a given component
- Check `ResourceStore::Exists( id )` before calling `Get()` in non-critical paths
- Register `PhysicsSystem::Observer` for collision responses; don't poll physics state per frame
- Use `RenderSystem::CreateTexture()` for static sprite textures; pass the index to `AttachSprite()` or `AttachRenderable()`
- Use `RenderSystem::AttachSprite()` / `AttachRenderable()` helpers for common setup
- Hold shared mesh/material creators in `ResourceHandle` members; Reset on teardown

## DON'Ts

- Don't store raw pointers to components across frames -- dense pools can reallocate on `Remove`
- Don't call `PhysicsEngine` methods directly from game code -- go through `PhysicsSystem`
- Don't add engine-specific (graphics/audio/physics) includes to component headers -- keep them POD-friendly
- Don't manually `AddReference`/`RemoveReference` from game code for meshes/materials -- use handles and Attach/Detach
- Don't bind textures through `MaterialBuilder::AddTexture()` for sprites -- use `CreateTexture()` instead
